From af7c33e53ce004fbb9a6195090d4e07901597fc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: T3chnobone <98963290+T3chnobone@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:25:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/17] Add LAN netplay with up to 8 players

Deterministic lockstep over TCP: each PC runs the full game and the host
relays every player's input per frame. Includes a lobby window (host/join,
character pick, match type), start-state sync (seed, menu state, gameplay
CVars), compatibility checks and periodic desync detection.

Big race mode: a 1P Grand Prix where karts 2-8 are driven by other PCs and
each PC renders its own kart full-screen. Lifts the game's 4-human limits
(HUD, items, Lakitu, controllers, item use, pause, finish gate) and gives
every kart full physics. Split-screen mode keeps the classic 2-4 player view.

See docs/NETPLAY.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qq7B1uqfWVWykYRDDMiuXa
